Subject: adds regvm_step(), a one-instruction-at-a-time entry into the register interpreter

What this does
  Gives every register opcode a step form: a function that runs exactly one
  instruction with the interpreter's semantics and returns the next ip instead
  of dispatching further. The register interpreter's threaded handlers tail-call
  into their successor, so they cannot be called for a single instruction; this
  patch generates a step twin for each from the monolith (non-threaded) handler
  bodies and adds regvm_step() to dispatch through a regvm_step_table.

  Generated, not hand-written. tools are not shipped; the generator
  (emit-step.py) reads quickjs.c, extracts each ROP's monolith body, rewrites
  frame references to the JSRegRun passed in, and emits quickjs-regvm-step.inc,
  which is #included at the end of js_regvm_execute. Hand-written step forms
  cover the cases that are not one instruction: return (all three forms),
  yield/yield_star, await, initial_yield, and the unimplemented-opcode trap.

  QJS_REGVM_STEPCHECK=1 makes the monolith interpreter run every instruction
  through regvm_step() instead of its own dispatch loop, so the step forms are
  exercised under the full test262 suite before any native code is generated.
  That build reproduces the plain register build's test262 result exactly and
  the same box2d checksum.

Why we need it
  This is phase P1 of .local/aot-regvm-impl-plan.md. Compiled (AOT) code
  interleaves generated instructions with interpreter instructions, so it needs
  to run one ROP at a time and regain control after each; regvm_step() is that
  entry point. The step table also makes coverage explicit:
  regvm_step_uncovered() returns the count of ROPs with no step form (target 0).

What it adds
  quickjs-regvm-step.inc
      One regvm_s_<op>() per register opcode plus regvm_step_table[],
      regvm_step_covered[], regvm_step() and regvm_step_uncovered().
  quickjs.c
      Hoists the register-run types and REGVM_COLD_RET/REGVM_STEP_SUSPEND so
      the step forms compile in a non-threaded build; adds JSRegRun.caller_ctx
      (throws must use the caller's realm, not the callee's) and
      JSRegRun.resume_marker (yield/await resume target); adds the STEPCHECK
      loop at the monolith entry and the QJS_REGVM_STEPCHECK knob.

Nothing here is compiled without -DQJS_REGVM; without it the build is
unchanged.

